Nicholas Jackson interviewed an Anonymous Student for opinions on the meet up service

  Q: Have you ever struggled with deciding a place to meet with your friend/study partner that is fair for both parties? 
  A: Yes! Especially with UTD having such a large part of the student population that commutes. 
  It is tough to find places between us, especially when the metroplex is so large and traffic is unpredictable.

  Q: What kind of places do you like to meet up at?
  A: It really depends on what I'm meeting for. If I am studying, I usually stick to coffee shops, the library, or maybe someone's apartment/house. 
    When it is just to hangout, I frequent boba shops, dessert cafes, and parks. I'm also a big fan of trying new restaurants, especially Korean BBQ and poke bowls.

  Q: When deciding where to meet, are you more focused on overall mileage or overall time?
  A: Typically time. It feels like a better way to find a fair meeting place. Mileage only feels important if I am traveling somewhere 20+ miles away.

  Q: If there was app to assist with finding meeting places between two parties, how would you like it to function?
  A: I would like to be presented various options within like a 2 mile radius. It would be cool if the app promoted spots specifically for studying and different places for more social interactions.
    I think it would be important to have both ETA's be around the same time, and it would be nice to share the route directly to the other party. It would also be cool to see how well places are reviewed and maybe a menu link.

  Q: Do you have a preference between Google Maps and Apple Maps?
  A: I have an Android phone, so I only use Google Maps.

  Q: How do you deem a service as reliable?
  A: It would be a perfect world if everything worked 100% of the time. In terms of software, I think anywhere from a 95-98% success rate would be deemed highly reliable.

  Q: Would you like the service to create a profile and save information like addresses that you depart from frequently?
  A: I honestly do not like having to maintain a user/password for so many services. I also don't like the idea of a third party platform tracking my location. 
    With so much tracking and predictive measures in so many services, I wouldn't mind having one that didn't store my information.
